<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#lepontic-language">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lepontic language</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Lepontic</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lepontic is an ancient Celtic language known from about 140 inscriptions found around the Italian lakes and the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a>, dated from about the 6th to the 1st century BCE. It was written in an alphabet adapted from Etruscan and is linked to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golasecca-culture">Golasecca culture</a>. It is one of the earliest attested Celtic languages.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lepontic-language.jpg" alt="Lepontic language" width="320" height="216" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marco Zanoli (sidonius (talk) 22:00, 2 January 2009 (UTC)) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:R%C3%B6mische_Provinzen_im_Alpenraum_ca_14_n_Chr.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
